I was responsible for overall project coordination using a hybrid project management approach. A traditional schedule was used to define major milestones (design, implementation, testing and demonstration), while Agile principles were applied within each phase through short iterative development cycles. Tasks were tracked using a GitHub issue board, allowing progress monitoring, prioritization, and dependency management across team members. This approach ensured timely delivery while remaining flexible to technical changes during development.
I designed the system architecture and data flow for the project. This included defining how log data moves from ingestion through preprocessing, aggregation, policy enforcement, and output. An architecture diagram was created to clearly show component interactions, data dependencies, and integration points. This documentation helped align development across all modules and ensured consistent implementation.
I set up and managed the GitHub repository workflow. This included configuring a protected main branch, enforcing branch rules, and defining a pull request (PR) template to maintain code quality. A clear branching strategy was introduced to support parallel development and safe integration. Member 1 also handled merge coordination, resolving conflicts and ensuring that all components worked together correctly.
I also led the system integration process, combining outputs from preprocessing, enforcement, and testing modules into a unified workflow. A structured demo script was created to demonstrate system functionality, including log ingestion, detection logic, enforcement actions, and output results. This ensured the final demonstration was clear, repeatable, and aligned with project requirements.
